  "notes": "SIMILAR WORDS:\n{黙読|もくどく} (silent reading) is the opposite of {音読|おんどく} (reading aloud). In Japanese schools, both are practiced. {音読|おんどく} is emphasized in language learning because it helps with pronunciation and retention, while {黙読|もくどく} is used for comprehension exercises.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {黙読|もくどく}する (to read silently)\n- {黙読|もくどく}で{読|よ}む (to read by silent reading)\n- {黙読|もくどく}の{時間|じかん} (silent reading time)\n\nWRITING:\n{黙|もく} means silence, as in {沈黙|ちんもく} (silence). {読|どく} means reading.",
